nue doing our jobs so you don't  think it's exactly connected that this  is the last chance of duterte to issue  something like this well it is not for  me to say but we can probably connect  the dots on our own and i would say that  in this country and well anywhere in the  world nothing really happens without a  political connection  so you can intelligently deduce that  well  it might have something to do with it  and well  all we have to do is to roll with the  punches  what does this decision mean for free  media in the philippines  well uh obviously this is an  attack  against  breast freedom  because rappler has been  just doing its job as as a journalist as  the fourth estate and um well if people  other media other journalists would see  how rapper is being treated  it might  you know scare them or  you know they might shy away from doing  critical stories and i think that is the  the biggest impact of this on the the  industry it creates a chilling effect  rappler is um unaffected by this uh  chilling effect we continue to do our  jobs  as best as we can but you know other  media outlets might not be  might be more vulnerable than us because  of the corporate structure of  the the other media outlets owned by big  businessmen controlled by big  businessmen rappler is  lucky to have this  environment that fosters  free  independent reporting but you know the  effect on the others  it really creates a chilling effect and  that is  what worries us and worries many  watchdogs around the world  so you can still work  of course it's not a question of we can  can we still work i mean it's never a  question uh  our newsroom is uh bustling today our  eyes are set on the goal which is to  report  dark days for press freedom thanks very  much thank you very much  you
 

